      "batch_node": {
        "source": "plugins.git_serious.grift.landing",
        "name": "git-serious landing v0.5.0",
        "description": "Second light (git-serious-tap#6): the observed account's CI/CD system as one legible picture. Structure is containment — account ⊃ repositories ⊃ workflows — drawn by the plugin's landing layout module (static/git_serious/js/projections/landing.js) over the same node seed as v0.1.0; the GitHub Apps and the Actions OIDC issuer sit in a row beneath the account with their ENABLED_ON edges kept. The status wall rides the graph as status badges on the workflow cards (req-git-serious-status-wall): red = failed runs in the collected window, grey = no run observed for this workflow at all. Three states, never two: a card with no badge means every collected run passed; a grey badge means we could not say. Runs and jobs stay off the canvas. GitHub nodes single-tap to their html_url. v0.3.0 adds the status wall AS TABLES beneath the graph (req-git-serious-status-wall-1, the first table-stakes table): every collected run across every repository, newest first, and beneath it the workflows with no run in the collected window. Both are envelope-mode Gryphon searches bound to standard table panels — a page and a query, no code — so any consumer can mount the same pair on its own page with one USES_PANEL edge. The wall is account-wide by definition; the graph above is this org's machinery. The collected window is github_core's initial_run_limit (10 runs per REPOSITORY), so 'no run observed' here means 'no run inside that window', never 'this workflow never ran' — the panel text says so. Re-publish of v0.2.0: page, panel, projection, elevation, layout and search ids are stable; only the batch id moved. v0.4.0 (2026-09-02): the landing graph IS the machinery view of the primary repository (github_core's machinery projection module; git-serious-tap#35) — the account-wide picture lives on /git-serious/org. Node upserts only: the layout's js_file, the projection's `machinery` key, and the node search's scoped query; edges are untouched because the importer keys an edge on its endpoints. The status-wall tables beneath are unchanged. v0.4.1: the graph row takes 9fr of 12 (~75% of the page) while the machinery view is being dialed in. v0.5.0 (wall port onto the machinery landing): the page scrolls — the graph keeps 75vh, the tables take fixed heights (640 / 360 px, Tabulator-owned scroll, sticky header); the wall's columns are the trigger as a glyph (TAP's CI-universal trigger icons mapped from GitHub's event vocabulary), run number linking to the run, branch linking to the repository's branch page, conclusion, viewer-local started/completed, Elapsed with the ratio to the median of the other successful runs of the same workflow and trigger (outlier / within / not enough history), and a history link to the workflow page (/git-serious/workflow?workflow_id=…, git-serious-tap#41). Re-publish: every id stable; only the batch id moved."
      },
      "nodes": [
        {
          "entity": {
            "entity_id": "01a03f78-11fa-7029-823d-7944e18dd24a",
